s θ, sin θ) on the unit circle\",\n    \"concept\": \"trig\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"unit circle\",\n      \"unit circle\",\n      \"sine\",\n      \"cosine\",\n      \"trigonometry\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"angleDeg\",\n        \"label\": \"Angle\",\n        \"unit\": \"°\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 360,\n        \"default\": 105.86\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"geophysics-earth\",\n    \"route\": \"/geophysics/earth\",\n    \"subject\": \"Geophysics\",\n    \"title\": \"Earth explorer\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore layers of Earth and the atmosphere using the existing interactive model.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Layer properties change with depth and altitude\",\n    \"concept\": \"earth\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"earth\",\n      \"earth explorer\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"geophysics-lab\",\n    \"route\": \"/geophysics/lab\",\n    \"subject\": \"Geophysics\",\n    \"title\": \"Geophysics field lab\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare simplified gravity, resistivity, seismic and electromagnetic field models.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Measured physical signals can constrain subsurface models\",\n    \"concept\": \"geophysics\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"lab\",\n      \"geophysics field lab\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"geophysics-solar\",\n    \"route\": \"/geophysics/solar\",\n    \"subject\": \"Geophysics\",\n    \"title\": \"Solar system explorer\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore planet families, orbital behaviour and the nebular formation model.\",\n    \"principle\": \"For bodies orbiting the same central mass: T² ∝ a³\",\n    \"concept\": \"solar\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"solar\",\n      \"solar system explorer\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"geophysics-tectonics\",\n    \"route\": \"/geophysics/tectonics\",\n    \"subject\": \"Geophysics\",\n    \"title\": \"Plate tectonics\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore plates, boundaries, magnetic stripes, triple junctions and Earth’s shape.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Plate motion links surface patterns and geological processes\",\n    \"concept\": \"tectonics\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"tectonics\",\n      \"plate tectonics\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-damped-oscillator\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/damped-oscillator\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Damped oscillator\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore how damping changes oscillations and the approach to equilibrium.\",\n    \"principle\": \"A damping force removes mechanical energy\",\n    \"concept\": \"oscillation\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"damped oscillator\",\n      \"damped oscillator\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"gamma\",\n        \"label\": \"Damping γ\",\n        \"unit\": \"1/s\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 6,\n        \"default\": 0.8\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"omega0\",\n        \"label\": \"Natural frequency ω₀\",\n        \"unit\": \"rad/s\",\n        \"min\": 0.5,\n        \"max\": 6,\n        \"default\": 2\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"y0\",\n        \"label\": \"Initial displacement y(0)\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": -2,\n        \"max\": 2,\n        \"default\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"yp0\",\n        \"label\": \"Initial velocity y'(0)\",\n        \"unit\": \"/s\",\n        \"min\": -4,\n        \"max\": 4,\n        \"default\": 0\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-div-stokes\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/div-stokes\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Divergence and Stokes theorems\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare local derivative descriptions with flux and circulation integrals.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Volume divergence corresponds to closed-surface flux\",\n    \"concept\": \"calculus\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"div stokes\",\n      \"divergence and stokes theorems\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"disk.r\",\n        \"label\": \"disk.r\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0.4,\n        \"max\": 2.2,\n        \"default\": 1.1\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-eigenvector-explorer\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/eigenvector-explorer\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Eigenvector explorer\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore directions preserved by a linear transformation.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Av = λv for a nonzero eigenvector v\",\n    \"concept\": \"matrix\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"eigenvector explorer\",\n      \"eigenvector explorer\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"t\",\n        \"label\": \"t\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 1,\n        \"default\": 1\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-fourier-series\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/fourier-series\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Fourier series\",\n    \"description\": \"Build a periodic signal from harmonic components.\",\n    \"principle\": \"A periodic signal can be represented by harmonic sums under suitable conditions\",\n    \"concept\": \"fourier\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"fourier series\",\n      \"fourier series\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"n\",\n        \"label\": \"n\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 1,\n        \"max\": 60,\n        \"default\": 1,\n        \"integer\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-fourier-transform\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/fourier-transform\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Fourier transform\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare a signal with its frequency-domain representation.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Frequency-domain structure describes a signal’s component frequencies\",\n    \"concept\": \"fourier\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"fourier transform\",\n      \"fourier transform\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"a\",\n        \"label\": \"a\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0.2,\n        \"max\": 3,\n        \"default\": 1\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-gamma-function\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/gamma-function\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Gamma function\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore how the gamma function extends factorials beyond positive integers.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Γ(n) = (n−1)! for positive integers n\",\n    \"concept\": \"special\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"gamma function\",\n      \"gamma function\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-gradient-explorer\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/gradient-explorer\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Gradient explorer\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore how a scalar field changes and how its gradient points uphill.\",\n    \"principle\": \"∇f points in the direction of greatest local increase\",\n    \"concept\": \"calculus\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"gradient explorer\",\n      \"gradient explorer\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-hermite-laguerre-delta\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/hermite-laguerre-delta\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Hermite, Laguerre and delta\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore special functions and finite-width representations of a delta distribution.\",\n    \"principle\": \"A delta distribution is defined through its action under integration\",\n    \"concept\": \"special\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"hermite laguerre delta\",\n      \"hermite, laguerre and delta\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"epsExp\",\n        \"label\": \"epsExp\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": -2,\n        \"max\": 0.3,\n        \"default\": 0\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-legendre-bessel\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/legendre-bessel\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Legendre and Bessel functions\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore special-function solutions that arise in problems with symmetry.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Boundary conditions select physically relevant solutions\",\n    \"concept\": \"special\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"legendre bessel\",\n      \"legendre and bessel functions\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"besX\",\n        \"label\": \"besX\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0.5,\n        \"max\": 14.5,\n        \"default\": 5\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"biology-skeletal-system\",\n    \"route\": \"/biology/skeletal-system\",\n    \"subject\": \"Biology\",\n    \"title\": \"Human skeletal system\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore the major bones and groups, their locations and functions. A typical adult has 206 bones: 80 axial and 126 appendicular. Group counts are not counts of SVG shapes. Identification and classification challenges support classroom discussion.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Axial (80) + appendicular (126) = 206 bones in a typical adult. Bones support, protect and act as levers.\",\n    \"concept\": \"skeleton\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"skeletal system\",\n      \"human skeleton\",\n      \"skeleto